"**HMS\u202fSharpshooter \u2013 Commanders who held the ship and had been awarded the Distinguished Service Order (DSO) before the end of WWII**\n\n| Commander | Rank during command | Period as CO of\u202fHMS\u202fSharpshooter | DSO award (date if known) | Source |\n|-----------|---------------------|----------------------------------|----------------------------|---------|\n| **Lieutenant\u2011Commander David Lampen** | Lt\u2011Cdr. (later Cmdr.) | 15\u202fOct\u202f1940 \u2013 20\u202fMay\u202f1942 | 25\u202fAug\u202f1942 \u2013 *for skill and coolness in successful actions against enemy submarines while serving aboard HMS\u202fSharpshooter* | [laststandonzombieisland.com](https://laststandonzombieisland.com/tag/hms-sharpshooter-j68/) \u2013 \u201cMeanwhile, her skipper, LCDR David Lampen received the DSO on 25\u202fAugust \u2026\u201d |\n| **Lieutenant\u2011Commander Robert Bill** | Lt\u2011Cdr. (DSO) | 1\u202fJun\u202f1945 \u2013 31\u202fJul\u202f1945 | *Earlier* (exact date not listed in the source; he already had the DSO before assuming command) | [uboat.net \u2013 HMS\u202fSharpshooter](https://uboat.net/allies/warships/ship/3674.html) \u2013 \u201cLt.Cdr. Robert Bill, DSO, RN Jun\u202f1945\u202f31\u202fJul\u202f1945\u201d |\n\n**How we arrived at this list**\n\n1. The definitive list of HMS\u202fSharpshooter\u2019s commanding officers during WWII is given on the U\u2011Boat\u202fNet \u201cHMS\u202fSharpshooter\u201d page.  It shows seven commanders in total, including their tenure periods and any medals they carried at the time.  \n2. From this list, only two officers carried the abbreviation **DSO**: David Lampen (who had **DSO** after his acts in 1942) and Robert Bill (who already possessed the DSO when he took command).  \n3. We confirmed Lampen\u2019s DSO award date through the\u202flaststand\u2011on\u2011zombie\u2011island article, which cites the award on 25\u202fAugust 1942 for actions against *U\u2011655*.  \n4. For Bill, the U\u2011Boat\u202fNet listing explicitly names him as \u201cRobert Bill, DSO, RN\u201d for his commandeering period in mid\u20111945, indicating he had received the award earlier.\n\n**Summary**\n\nDuring the period from the outbreak of WWII (September\u202f1939) until Germany\u2019s surrender on 8\u202fMay\u202f1945, only two commanding officers of HMS\u202fSharpshooter had been recognized with the Distinguished Service Order: Lieutenant\u2011Commander David Lampen and Lieutenant\u2011Commander Robert Bill.  No other commanding officers of the vessel during that timeframe held the DSO."